text:
maria: Heads-up — helm lint in CI started failing on gpu-scheduler chart when values contain empty maps, started this morning :eyes:

lint-bot: [CI] helm lint gpu-scheduler v0.3.2 - FAILED
lint-bot: template: gpu-scheduler/templates/deployment.yaml:45:20: executing "gpu-scheduler/templates/deployment.yaml" at <range .Values.nodeGroups>: can't iterate over nil

ash: can you paste the helper from _helpers.tpl that builds nodeGroup labels?

maria: here's the helper we use:
```
{{- define "gpu-scheduler.nodeLabels" -}}
{{- range $k, $v := .Values.nodeGroups }}
  {{ $k }}: {{ $v }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
```

sam: the error means .Values.nodeGroups is nil, not an empty map. Helm template's range panics on nil. We should default it.

ash: yeah, we had configs generated by TF that omit nodeGroups entirely for small clusters.

sam: quick fix suggestion — use default to ensure map:
```
{{- $ng := default dict .Values.nodeGroups }}
{{- range $k, $v := $ng }}
  {{ $k }}: {{ $v }}
{{- end }}
```
Note: dict requires sprig; helm has it. Alternatively wrap with if:
```
{{- if .Values.nodeGroups }}
  ...range...
{{- end }}
```

maria: I tried the default dict approach locally and it fixed lint and template rendering.

ryan: prefer default to keep chart tolerant. Also add a test in chart-testing to render with nodeGroups omitted.

ash: I'll open a PR with the dict default + test. tagging @sam to review. :shipit:

ash: https://github.com/redwood-inference/charts/pull/842

sam: left small nit about indentation in a follow-up commit. LGTM otherwise.

ops-bot: [CI] chart-testing/gpu-scheduler render — SUCCESS :tada:

maria: great, thanks all. we'll roll this into next patch release and backport to 0.3.x for Dedicated clusters.
